              "text": "If you are looking for **free satellite radio**, your options depend on whether you want to access the popular **SiriusXM** service, use physical **Free-to-Air satellite hardware**, or listen to **free digital radio alternatives**. \n\n---\n\n### 1. The SiriusXM \"Free Access\" Plan (Ad-Supported)\nSiriusXM offers a **Free Access Plan**. This is a completely free, ad-supported tier that does not require a subscription fee or a credit card.\n\n* **How it works:** It offers a selection of music, talk, comedy, sports, and news channels with commercial breaks (similar to AM/FM radio).\n* **The catch:** \n  * It is only available in-car (it does not work on the SiriusXM phone app).\n  * It only works on eligible, newer vehicles equipped with **SiriusXM 360L hybrid radios** (typically found on select models from Ford, Chevrolet, GMC, Cadillac, Dodge, Nissan, Volvo, and Subaru).\n  * You must use the radio **at least once every 60 days** to keep the free subscription active. \n* **How to get it:** If your car is compatible, a \"Free Access\" welcome or opt-in screen will eventually appear on your vehicle\u2019s dashboard touchscreen.\n\n---\n\n### 2. SiriusXM Free Trials & Partner Promotions\nIf you do not have a 360L-capable vehicle, you can still get SiriusXM for free using introductory trials and promotional deals:\n\n* **No-Credit-Card In-Car Trials:** SiriusXM frequently runs promotions offering **3 months of free in-car listening** for inactive factory-installed radios. Many of these promotions do not require you to enter a credit card, meaning you won't be charged when the trial ends.\n* **Dealer Trials:** If you buy a new or certified pre-owned car, it almost always comes with a free trial ranging from **3 to 12 months** (depending on the auto manufacturer).\n* **Partner Offers:** Major companies often bundle free streaming trials of SiriusXM with their products:\n  * **Samsung:** Offers **6 months of free SiriusXM Streaming** to new subscribers (often tied to buying a phone or redeeming via Samsung Members).\n  * **T-Mobile / Sprint:** Frequently offers T-Mobile customers **6 months of free SiriusXM Streaming Platinum**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. SiriusXM National \"Free Listening\" Events\nA few times a year, SiriusXM hosts **Free Listening Events** (usually during holiday weekends like Memorial Day, Labor Day, and Thanksgiving). \nDuring these events, they temporarily unencrypt their satellite signal. If you have an inactive satellite radio in your car, all you have to do is turn it on to listen to dozens of free channels\u2014no sign-up, credit card, or activation required.\n\n---\n\n### 4. True \"Free-to-Air\" (FTA) Satellite Radio\nIf you are referring to literal satellite hardware rather than the SiriusXM brand, you can set up a **Free-to-Air (FTA) satellite receiver**.\n* By installing a satellite dish pointed at certain satellites (such as **Galaxy 19** at 97\u00b0 West) and using a DVB-S/S2 satellite box, you can pull in hundreds of completely unencrypted, free international TV and radio stations. \n* This method is entirely legal and requires zero monthly fees, though it does require a one-time purchase of the dish and receiver.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Free Digital Radio Alternatives (Internet-Based)\nIf you want the variety and curation of satellite radio without paying anything, internet-based streaming radio is the most popular alternative. If you have a smartphone connected to your car's Bluetooth or Apple CarPlay/Android Auto, you can use:\n* **TuneIn:** Streams thousands of local and international AM/FM radio stations, plus talk and sports.\n* **iHeartRadio:** Offers free access to hundreds of live broadcast radio stations across the country.\n* **AccuRadio:** A completely free internet radio service with hundreds of highly customizable music channels and unlimited skips.\n* **Radio Garden:** A highly unique, interactive globe interface that lets you spin the earth and tune into live local radio broadcasts from anywhere in the world for free.",
